WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.250
Let's have a nice clean game.everyone.

2
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.110
Down.

3
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.330
Come on.move the puck.
Wendell! Move it! Move the puck!

4
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.270
Up here.Booth. Up here!

5
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.540
Back on D.

6
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.490
Pick 'em up.on D. pick 'em up.

7
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.740
Go.Booth! Go.Booth! Go.Booth!

8
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.210
Kill 'em.Booth!

9
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.320
What did he do that for?

10
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.730
It's what Booth does.
Keeps the other team honest.

11
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.080
He's what you call an enforcer.

12
00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.810
What.like law enforcement?

13
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.180
Yeah.okay. Well.let's go with that.

14
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.190
Oh.what was that? What about the
cross-check? Ref.are you blind?

15
00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.170
Pass it! I'm open! Pass it! I'm open!

16
00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.200
Pick him off! Yeah!

17
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.630
That was a cheap shot.Carlson.

18
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.260
Yeah.you guys suck.

19
00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.200
That's 24 Blue. two
minutes for charging.

20
00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.040
For what?

21
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.120
- What about the cross-check
back there.huh? - Get in the box!

22
00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.640
Come on.man. It's hockey.

23
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.310
Club hockey.and some of us have to
go work in the morning. all right.pal?

24
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.080
- Enough. Let's go.
- Carlson.clam down! Skate away.

25
00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.720
- Just go in the box.
- Go on. get in there and sit down.

26
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.140
- Yeah.sit down.crybaby.
- Let's go.

27
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.940
Let's go.

28
00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.000
So.this is punitive. right?

29
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.930
To be sent to this little area here?

30
00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.760
Keep your head up next time.
number 12. Keep your head up.

31
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.530
Yeah.yeah.I'll be waiting.

32
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.210
Come on!

33
00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.320
It's called a penalty
box. you know.send in.

34
00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:44.640
Yeah.Booth committed a penalty when he checked
the big guy when he didn't have the puck.

35
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.930
Stay with him.Paul. Just stay with him.

36
00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.980
There's a hit right there.Ref.
that you missed again.

37
00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.970
Booth seems quite anxious to
get out of the disciplinary box.

38
00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.930
Yeah.I've never seen
him this agitated before.

39
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.280
Open man! Open man!

40
00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.270
- That's not good.right?
- No.

41
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.710
Go.Booth!

42
00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.550
Wendell might get a basket!

43
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.510
Elbow.Ref! Elbow!

44
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.710
Is Wendell okay?

45
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.860
That can't be legal.

46
00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.130
It definitely is not.

47
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.330
- Come on.Ref. you got to call
- Come on.what are you doing.Carlson?

48
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.730
Want to go?

49
00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.110
Come on. come on. Let's
go. Come on.let's go.

50
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.300
Come on.Booth!

51
00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.590
You're a dirty player.Carlson.

52
00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:49.230
Come on.bro. Get your hands
free. Get your hands free.

53
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:55.590
You don't take shots at my
guys. You got that? Ends here.

54
00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.720
Okay.Carlson?

55
00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:01.850
Ends here.

56
00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.120
Booth seems to be winning.

57
00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.040
Well.it's Booth I'm worried about.

58
00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.200
- That guy's out of control.
- No more.

59
00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.740
I'm gonna have to call a
game misconduct on that one.

60
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.300
All right. You get up off the ice.we'll
finish this in the parking lot. Come on.

61
00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:17.030
If you did your job.I wouldn't
have to do it for you. Look at him.

62
00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.530
- He's hitting my guys.
- You all right.buddy?

63
00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.810
Son of a bitch.

64
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.680
Get up. You all right?

65
00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.420
Oh.did I score.man?

66
00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.420
Oh.yeah. Yeah... Come on.

67
00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.110
I do not know how I feel about this.

68
00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.150
It's very primal.

69
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.270
I like it just a little too much.

70
00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:44.030
- Come on.team.
- All right.come on.let's focus.

71
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.430
So.you still seeing double?

72
00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.980
Only when I open more than one eye.

73
00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.680
Your hand's busted.

74
00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:56.280
Yeah.well.you know.
guy left his helmet on.

75
00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.080
Hey.you two all right?

76
00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.810
- What?
- Want to wait outside?

77
00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.630
But your hand might be broken.
Do you want me to look at it?

78
00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.750
No.it's all right. You
can wait outside please.

79
00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.750
It's a men's locker room.Bones.

80
00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:29.350
There comes a time in ice fishing when it's time
for the father to turn the drilling over to his son.

81
00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.180
Man.this is a great day.

82
00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.950
- You give me a beer. let me run the augur.
- Yup.

83
00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.450
You're 18.Leo.

84
00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.700
You start drilling
holes. it's safety first.

85
00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.490
- You got me?
- Yeah.

86
00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.530
Nothing I'm saying here
applies only to ice augurs.

87
00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.360
You get me?

88
00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.190
- All right.
- Good.

89
00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:59.170
You know.that way. you don't fall through the
ice and die. or get a disease. or get pregnant.

90
00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.520
- Dad.come on.
- Okay.

91
00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.910
- Go ahead.
- All right.

92
00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:09.190
That a boy. Keep her perpendicular.

93
00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.610
Once you get it in a little bit.
you can speed her up.let her rip.

94
00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.840
All right.let her rip.

95
00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.150
Dad.she-she's bleeding.

96
00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.660
- I... she's bleeding.
- Pull out. Pull out.

97
00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.060
Oh.I hope that's fish.

98
00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.200
You better go wait in the truck.

99
00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.260
Hey.uh.what do you think there.Bones?

100
00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:48.290
I would surmise that the body went into the
lake before it froze.then the lake froze.

101
00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:52.310
then the body floated up and became
attached to the bottom of the ice.

102
00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.770
I meant.was he murdered?

103
00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.980
Um.maybe.

104
00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.040
Could have been an accident
or a suicide.except...

105
00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.050
- Oh.you shouldn't do that.
- It itches.okay?

106
00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:06.000
Yeah.well.except for what?

107
00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:10.730
Trauma to the left maxillary
orbit suggests violence.

108
00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.000
It's kind of gross. what you're doing.

109
00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:15.200
Gross? You got your finger
in some guy's maxillary orbit.

110
00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.070
I don't think there's anything
else to be learned here.

111
00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.760
so let's get this
Popsicle back to the lab.

112
00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.170
Hey.look at that. Bones.you made a joke.

113
00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.830
Well.I can be quite amusing.

114
00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.420
Wait a second.

115
00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:30.120
Booth.you aren't wearing any gloves.

116
00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.780
Bones.I...

117
00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.060
Remember that guy I punched out
last month during my hockey game?

118
00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:41.270
- Pete Carlson?
- Yes. When you broke your hand.

119
00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:44.350
That's him.

120
00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:49.700
I'm a suspect. Here.

121
00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:26.980
<font color=#00FFFF>Bones Season04
Episode13 Fire in the Ice</font>

122
00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.300
Given that Agent Booth is currently
the prime suspect in this murder...

123
00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.800
We don't know it's a murder.

124
00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:37.710
Oh.look at that--
I'm the prime suspect.

125
00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.070
Agent Payton Perotta here will
be working with Dr. Brennan.

126
00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.960
I won't work the case without Booth.

127
00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:46.380
In that case. I invite Agent
Booth's continued participation.

128
00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.170
In the background as an advisor.

129
00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:53.320
Agent Payton Perotta has earned bachelors
degrees in both forensic science and criminology.

130
00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:57.120
Well.anything short of a doctorate
is virtually useless at my level.

131
00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:58.710
How would you like to proceed.darling?

132
00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:02.500
Well.it's pretty obvious. We definitely want
to interrogate the primary suspect.right?

133
00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.330
Yeah.

134
00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:13.030
Based on decomp. I'd put time of death
at about five days prior to freezing.

135
00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.240
Local cops say the lake
froze over three weeks ago.

136
00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.690
Aside from some dormant
anopheles mosquito larvae.

137
00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:20.800
I imagine whatever the water from the lake
tells us. it'll be through a microscope.

138
00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:24.490
If Booth is a suspect. then I should
be.too. This guy scrambled my brains.

139
00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:28.530
Your alibi is that you were seeing double
and being taken care of by your mother.

140
00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:32.130
I'll get on the fluid samples you
took from the lungs and esophagus.

141
00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.900
Could be the vic was drowned somewhere
else and then dumped in the lake.

142
00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.700
No. Drowning's not the way
Booth would kill someone.

143
00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:43.240
Not that I actually
suspect Booth. At all.

144
00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.980
Quit staring at me.

145
00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:56.750
In the course of the game.the
victim and I exchanged blows.

146
00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.110
Who initiated the fight?

147
00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.120
It was hockey.

148
00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.830
So.it was spontaneous combustion?

149
00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:04.700
The guy hit two of my players.
The-The ref-- he didn't catch that.

150
00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.150
And that made you angry?

151
00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:09.820
Not angry enough.you know. to chase
him down after the game and kill him.

152
00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:11.400
So.where did you go after the game?

153
00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.930
Uh.Bones drove me and
Wendell to the hospital.

154
00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.780
So.alibi that night or the next?

155
00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.810
Bones and I are just partners.

156
00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:26.120
Okay. Now you're answering questions
I had no intention of asking.

157
00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:30.930
Is it your contention that.uh. your argument
with the victim was constrained to the ice?

158
00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:32.730
That is my contention.

159
00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:37.010
'Cause I have a-a witness who
stated you told Carlson. and I quote.

160
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.390
"You get up off that ice. and we'll
settle this out in the parking lot."

161
00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.710
Trash talking.

162
00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.070
Let me cut to the chase here.

163
00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.910
- Did you kill Pete Carlson?
- No.

164
00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.460
Did you dump his body in the lake?

165
00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:51.770
No.I did not.Agent Perotta.

166
00:09:55.460 --> 00:10:01.890
Do you feel that your experience as the child of an
abusive alcoholic has made you more prone to violence?

167
00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.690
Excuse me.

168
00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.030
What the hell are you doing?

169
00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.270
It's part of my job to assist
the interrogating agent.

170
00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.920
You know I didn't murder
anyone. Sweets.all right?

171
00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.160
So what you're doing right
now is you're just studying me.

172
00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:22.590
That's part of our agreement.too.

173
00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.490
You have a question for
me. you ask me yourself.

174
00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.590
Don't use her.

175
00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.170
All right.okay.two questions.

176
00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:31.110
One: am I picking up some sexual
tension between you and Agent Perotta?

177
00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.850
How the hell do I know
what you're picking up?

178
00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:38.530
Okay.Uh.two: underneath
your affable exterior

179
00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:41.960
is a deep reservoir of rage.

180
00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:45.260
My question is.do you always
have that under control?

181
00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:48.610
You know.if I didn't. you'd be dead
right now instead of just wincing.

182
00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:52.200
- I'm not wincing.
- Don't ever bring my old man up again.

183
00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.280
Rats. I winced.

184
00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:08.460
So...

185
00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:13.940
Doyouhave any more questions? Thank you.

186
00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.960
Yeah. You work out much?

187
00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:18.620
Yeah.I'm pretty consistent.

188
00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.820
You look like you take
excellent care of yourself.

189
00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.240
Okay.this is useless.

190
00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.530
Both patellas are fractured.

191
00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.180
As though he'd fallen to his knees?

192
00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.060
Yeah.with a great deal of force.

193
00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:35.250
During a hockey game?

194
00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:36.990
No.not if he wore pads.

195
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.020
I believe that this
is the cause of death.

196
00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:45.250
Penetration of the lachrymal sac here.deep
into the inferior orbital fissure.

197
00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.660
Yeah.I would have thought
a small caliber bullet.but...

198
00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:50.140
- No sign of bullet fragments.
- Yeah.

199
00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:56.390
This is Pete's apartment.

200
00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.360
He wasn't the best housekeeper.

201
00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.170
Ms. Withers.was Mr. Carlson
up to date on his rent?

202
00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.540
Good question. Great start.

203
00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:06.040
Uh.yes. Mostly.

204
00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.740
500 bucks short.

205
00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:11.410
He didn't need much. He
was a big kid at heart.

206
00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:13.720
Poor Pete.

207
00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.070
What he really loved was hockey.

208
00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:19.840
I wouldn't be surprised if that's why
he joined the volunteer fire department.

209
00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.550
I even got him this necklace.

210
00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:26.680
Crossed hockey sticks.

211
00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:28.460
You attended his games?

212
00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.440
Oh.all of them. Yeah.

213
00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:32.990
You were a couple?

214
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.710
It looks like someone went through all of his
belongings and then left them on the floor.

215
00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.130
Oh.it always looked like that.

216
00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:42.000
The car outside with the
flat tires.is that his?

217
00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:45.040
Yeah.somebody slashed the tires
just before he disappeared.

218
00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:46.720
Why didn't you report him missing?

219
00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:49.340
I thought maybe.uh...

220
00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:52.210
I thought he was staying
with someone else.

221
00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:53.500
There's a lot of bills here.

222
00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:55.240
"Final notice.past due..."

223
00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:58.280
Looks like he couldn't afford
to feed his fish.either.

224
00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:01.540
"Albie.Thursday.11:00 p.m."

225
00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.550
Do you know who Albie is?

226
00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:06.100
I don't know.

227
00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.860
This is blood.

228
00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.030
It's a hockey jersey.Bones.

229
00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.450
You know.hockey players bleed
sometimes when they play the game.

230
00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:13.880
Ms. Withers.how bad were
his financial problems?

231
00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:19.440
Well.a couple days before Pete
disappeared. he asked me for $2.000.

232
00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.500
Did he say what for?

233
00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:24.180
He liked me. You know?

234
00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.330
He was one of these guys.he...

235
00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:30.030
he didn't say much. but
he could be real sweet.

236
00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:35.410
And a man borrows money from a woman.
it means there's a bond of trust.right?

237
00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.210
I don't understand your reasoning.

238
00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:41.210
I do. It's definitely a bond of
trust. You're absolutely right.

239
00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:44.140
We're terribly sorry for your loss.

240
00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.730
Is that our victim?

241
00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:56.190
Yes. The last of the tissue samples.

242
00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.940
Wendell can clean the skeleton
now and you can do your thing.

243
00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:03.170
You still think cause of death was
a projectile through the left eye?

244
00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:08.250
Yes.but since we found no bullet.nor any
indication of gunpowder residue in the wound.

245
00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:10.210
we're stumped as to
what kind of projectile.

246
00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:15.350
The alveolus around the incisor is
cracked. the socket caked with blood.

247
00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.290
This is a recent loss.

248
00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:18.970
Well.he was a hockey player.

249
00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.120
So basically. we're
talking about gladiators.

250
00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.680
And I love it.

251
00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:27.250
Perhaps the sight of males battling
stimulates the part of your brain

252
00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:30.510
which has so far failed
to find a suitable mate.

253
00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:32.830
And thank God you're here.

254
00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:36.210
The water I found in the victim's
esophagus. not from the lake.

255
00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.480
Lake water is microorganism infested.

256
00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:40.910
Water in his
throat.deionized brine water.

257
00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.560
He was killed. then dumped in
the ocean then dumped in the lake?

258
00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:46.130
Deionized brine water freezes clear.

259
00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.960
It contains an antifreezing agent.which
I know sounds counterintuitive...

260
00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.620
Ice rinks.

261
00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:53.690
Kind of jumped my
punch line there.Dr. B.

262
00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.320
But.yes. We should see what
rinks are closest to the lake.

263
00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.140
It's the one Booth played at.

264
00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:03.080
I find it interesting that the
evidence keeps pointing toward Booth.

265
00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:23.990
Pete Carlson was murdered?

266
00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.360
Pete.he's indestructible.

267
00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:26.830
Not so indestructible.

268
00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.670
This guy took him down a few notches.

269
00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.030
Made him stay down.too.

270
00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:32.490
Well.it was the heat of the game.
All right.your guy crossed the line.

271
00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.900
He was our enforcer.
Took the job real serious.

272
00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.540
Well.whoever got Pete
must've got a drop on him.

273
00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:38.710
Pete wouldn't go easy.

274
00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:41.030
You mind my asking why
nobody reported him missing?

275
00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:44.000
Well.the night after you flattened
Pete. we go up against the State Police.

276
00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:46.660
Then Pete gets into a beef with
a big State Police left-winger.

277
00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:50.970
'Cause you handed him his ass on a platter.
Pete maybe had something to prove that night.

278
00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:52.500
You got a name?

279
00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.610
Hey.Alex? Yo! Come here!

280
00:15:57.050 --> 00:16:00.210
The fuzz player that Pete got into it with
his last game.do you remember his name?

281
00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:02.070
Yeah.Lou Herrin. number five.

282
00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:05.280
Pete took Herrin down with a real cheap shot.
He got tossed out the rest of the season.

283
00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:09.210
Any chance that Pete and this guy.Herrin.
continued their fight off the ice?

284
00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:10.240
People threaten.

285
00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:11.620
Yeah.but nobody carries through.

286
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.620
Yeah.keep it on the ice.right?

287
00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.350
If I were you.I would talk to Chloe.

288
00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:19.070
- Who's Chloe?
- Chloe Bratton.

289
00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.420
Chloe's a puck bunny.

290
00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.070
Here and Pete put in some quality
mattress time before he dumped her.

291
00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.010
Well.mattress really
isn't. uh.Chloe's style.

292
00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:27.710
- No offense.
- None taken.

293
00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.750
I favor backseats myself.

294
00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:38.140
I can't believe Pete's gone.

295
00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:40.040
How long ago did you two break up?

296
00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:43.190
Break up? We didn't break up.

297
00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:44.910
His teammates think you did.

298
00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:49.260
No.we had this on-again/off-again
thing. It was casual. No biggie.

299
00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.760
So you didn't mind that he
slept with different women?

300
00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:56.220
I wouldn't have minded if he did.
but I happen to know he didn't.

301
00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:59.530
Well.I happen to know
that he did. Right.

302
00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.140
- Who?
- t doesn't matter.does it?

303
00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:04.270
Given that your relationship
was so.um. casual?

304
00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:06.390
You slashed his tires. didn't you?

305
00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:07.810
- Agent Booth...
- No.

306
00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:11.640
We can prove you did it. Chloe.so here's
the deal: you tell us the truth from now on.

307
00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:15.780
and we won't charge you with vandalism
and obstruction of justice.okay?

308
00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:17.530
- Let's try it again. You slashed...
- Agent Booth?

309
00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:19.870
Yes. Of course.

310
00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:21.550
Let's try this again.

311
00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:23.510
You slashed his tires.didn't you?

312
00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:26.470
Yes.

313
00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:29.400
I mean.he was sleeping
with someone else.

314
00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:32.510
I got passions that take over sometimes.

315
00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:36.510
You know how it is when the guy you give
yourself to just goes off with someone else.

316
00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:40.250
Who's.um.Albie?

317
00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:42.380
Albie?

318
00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:46.790
Albie runs this poker game in back
of a Chinese food joint off I Street.

319
00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:49.350
Probably why Pete was
broke all the time.

320
00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.710
So.who'd you say Pete was sleeping with?

321
00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.580
I think we've got enough
information for today. Ms. Bratton.

322
00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.140
Thank you very much
for your cooperation.

323
00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.070
Thanks.

324
00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.460
Any luck with the murder weapon?

325
00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.970
Yes. We are certain it
is not a screwdriver.

326
00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:09.140
Well.the blood on the victim's
jersey was all his own.

327
00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:11.900
The rib cage has been bruised.

328
00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:14.190
- It has?
- Yes.

329
00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:17.360
See this vague pattern of bone bruising?

330
00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:21.950
Yeah.it extends from the right clavicle
through anterior ribs four through eight.

331
00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:24.770
He was struck repeatedly.

332
00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.480
Like.by a hockey stick?

333
00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:27.730
During the game maybe?

334
00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:31.000
Not during. The.um.padding would
prevent that kind of bruising.

335
00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:35.690
I'll take a closer look. I
can't believe I missed that.

336
00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:47.250
No.I can't believe
you missed that.either.

337
00:18:55.570 --> 00:19:00.380
I was signaling you to encourage Wendell
by saying anyone could've missed that.but...

338
00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:02.110
You should have said so.

339
00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:05.150
Booth says I stink at
nonverbal communication.

340
00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:09.200
She said in the back.

341
00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:13.210
Okay.well.just don't be pulling your
gun until you go through the kitchen.

342
00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:17.220
or Mama-san there is going to
hit the panic button. Okay.just...

343
00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:25.650
Ah.so you're ready to risk a gun fight
with your weapon in the wrong hand?

344
00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.430
I don't have a wrong hand.

345
00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:28.440
I'm curious.

346
00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:32.280
When you shoot with your left hand. does
it feel like somebody else is shooting?

347
00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:41.170
- What do we do now?
- Okay.FBI.

348
00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.890
Okay.I'd reach for my badge
right now. but.you know...

349
00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.250
Drop your weapons.please.

350
00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.440
"Please"? The FBI does not say "please."

351
00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:52.130
Okay.look. I really don't care
about the illegal gambling.

352
00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:58.050
I just want to talk to a guy named
Albie about a guy named Pete Carlson.

353
00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:06.260
I'm Albie.

354
00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:12.750
First rule: don't kill the
people who owe you money.

355
00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:14.940
All you get then is
trouble and no money.

356
00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:17.270
How much money did Carlson owe you?

357
00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:21.730
Okay.so you got your operation
shut down and moved out.

358
00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:26.470
because I can have my guys here in about
what.three minutes to mop that back room up?

359
00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:29.990
Pete Carlson was not a bad
player most of the time.but...

360
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.440
you know.every once in a while...

361
00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.160
He got brave and lost everything.huh?

362
00:20:33.190 --> 00:20:34.590
Gamble a bit yourself.do you?

363
00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:35.500
I'm reformed.

364
00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:38.760
Tell me.when was the last
time Carlson got.um.brave?

365
00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.230
Last month.

366
00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:42.220
But he paid up in full
a couple days later.

367
00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:44.120
Cash?

368
00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.060
Little garish. don't you think?

369
00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:53.970
I don't know where Pete got
it. but it covered his debt.

370
00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.540
I'm going to have to take this.

371
00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:58.600
If I didn't intend to give it
to you. you'd never have seen it.

372
00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:03.770
Okay.you gave me the time I needed to
move my operation. I gave you evidence.

373
00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.720
I call us square.

374
00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:09.480
You decide to get back into
the game. you look me up.

375
00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.740
Right. Yeah.

376
00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:15.270
Well.we gonna call this in?

377
00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:18.190
Oh.no point. Like the
woman said.she's moved on.

378
00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:26.590
Hodgins confirmed that the traces of
rink water in the victim's esophagus

379
00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:28.880
came from this rink.

380
00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.650
Well.how did rink ice
get into his throat?

381
00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:33.830
He was beaten.then a sharp
instrument was thrust into his eye.

382
00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:36.850
There should be blood stains.

383
00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:40.820
You're going to scan the
ice with one little wand?

384
00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:43.780
I'll call in an FBI forensics team.
We'll have the whole place searched.

385
00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:47.150
No need. All you need
is black light.right?

386
00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:48.720
- Yes.
- Right?

387
00:21:48.730 --> 00:21:52.770
I got a great idea. just stay here.
It's very slippery. don't move.

388
00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:57.610
Ready? How's that.huh?

389
00:21:57.620 --> 00:22:00.420
- Nice.
- Gonna work?

390
00:22:01.370 --> 00:22:04.260
Well.I see some.uh. flecks of blood.

391
00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:08.410
No we're looking for something bigger
than these small specs and spots.

392
00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:09.780
Uh.the victim was stabbed in the eye.

393
00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:11.680
We're looking for a
pretty significant puddle.

394
00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:14.240
Right.two guys get into a beef.then
they put their street clothes on

395
00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:17.580
and then come back here on
the ice to duke it out? No.

396
00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:20.160
- Booth?
- Yeah?

397
00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:23.240
My God.

398
00:22:23.250 --> 00:22:26.690
This is going to turn out to be
where Pete Carlson was murdered.

399
00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:41.340
This is all the ice from the crime scene.
including the scrapings from the Zamboni.

400
00:22:41.350 --> 00:22:45.860
We should be able to get enough DNA out
of this to confirm the blood is Carlson's.

401
00:22:46.900 --> 00:22:48.680
Human tooth.

402
00:22:48.690 --> 00:22:51.840
It's hockey. That Zamboni probably
had a hundred teeth in there.

403
00:22:54.550 --> 00:22:58.080
Looks like we found where
the Tooth Fairy winters.

404
00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:03.490
Did you find a match yet?

405
00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:04.700
Just started.

406
00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:07.040
Cam says it's definitely
the victim's blood.

407
00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:08.980
I still haven't found the murder weapon.

408
00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:13.190
Yeah.I know.I still haven't identified the
nylon polymer I found on the victim's shirt.

409
00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:17.490
So.I've looked at.like. a thousand photos
of those blood patterns at the rink.

410
00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:19.010
And tons from the apartment.

411
00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:20.140
Why.what are you looking for?

412
00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:22.170
Here's a blood pattern at the rink.

413
00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:24.500
The body was dragged in that direction.

414
00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:27.750
Yeah.the body was dragged that way.
but what are those drops over there?

415
00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:28.910
What drops?

416
00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:29.910
Those drops right there.

417
00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:33.600
They parallel the dragging
body. And they aren't smeared.

418
00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:36.420
These parallel drops
aren't from the victim.

419
00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:39.210
They're from whoever
dragged him across the ice.

420
00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:42.020
Well.that means we have to check
for more than just Pete's DNA.

421
00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:44.480
Too bad we can't question the fish.

422
00:23:45.380 --> 00:23:46.830
What killed those fish?

423
00:23:46.840 --> 00:23:48.570
Not eating for three weeks.

424
00:23:48.580 --> 00:23:50.900
If that happened. they
would eat each other.

425
00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:55.740
Grab your coat. We're
going on a field trip.

426
00:23:55.750 --> 00:24:00.060
And tell Cam to check the rink samples to
find out if there was a second source of DNA.

427
00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:02.670
I'm not really a big fan of this...

428
00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:05.900
barking out orders stuff.

429
00:24:11.020 --> 00:24:15.390
Agent Booth. it's come to the
attention of the deputy director

430
00:24:15.400 --> 00:24:18.300
that you are a viable
suspect in a murder case.

431
00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:22.120
Right.okay.and he wants you to
make sure that I'm not viable.

432
00:24:22.130 --> 00:24:22.890
That's correct.

433
00:24:22.910 --> 00:24:24.990
Come on.Sweets. you know
I didn't kill anyone.

434
00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:29.840
So.you know. put that in shrink talk and
write out your little form and send it in.

435
00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:35.190
Mm-hmm.yes.of course. but to do that.
I need to ask you some questions.

436
00:24:36.490 --> 00:24:39.390
Great. Shoot.

437
00:24:39.400 --> 00:24:41.860
I saw you in that game.

438
00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:43.790
You beat another man to the ice.

439
00:24:43.810 --> 00:24:45.920
It's hockey. I was
protecting my teammate.

440
00:24:45.930 --> 00:24:47.850
You broke your hand on his helmet.

441
00:24:47.880 --> 00:24:49.860
It's hockey.

442
00:24:49.870 --> 00:24:51.920
Okay.you never played.did you?

443
00:24:51.950 --> 00:24:57.360
Oh.I'd run track and cross country
and did some wrestling and ch...

444
00:24:58.420 --> 00:24:59.880
- Chess!
- No.

445
00:24:59.890 --> 00:25:01.510
- Checkers?
- Didn't say that.

446
00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:07.270
You know what? Then you know nothing...
It's about teams.okay? And teamwork.

447
00:25:07.280 --> 00:25:09.750
Obviously you don't know
anything about that. Dr. Sweets.

448
00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:12.710
You joined the army.

449
00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:14.510
You became a sniper.

450
00:25:14.530 --> 00:25:16.270
You joined the FBI.

451
00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:21.020
Do you see the.uh. the binding
element in those choices?

452
00:25:22.640 --> 00:25:23.870
It's violence.

453
00:25:23.900 --> 00:25:26.670
Or the love of uniforms.
You ever think that?

454
00:25:27.010 --> 00:25:33.450
Agent Booth. I believe that you
are ready to confront the fact that

455
00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:35.770
the violence you may
have suffered in childhood

456
00:25:35.780 --> 00:25:37.370
- You know what?
- has followed you into adulthood.

457
00:25:37.380 --> 00:25:40.130
Fill out the form.

458
00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:45.150
Not now!

459
00:25:45.160 --> 00:25:46.300
Hiya.Sweets.

460
00:25:46.330 --> 00:25:50.100
Uh.if you're about finished here.Booth. in
accordance with the warrant you made me get.

461
00:25:50.110 --> 00:25:51.680
Pete Carlson's phone records are here.

462
00:25:51.690 --> 00:25:54.450
Ms. Julian. actually.I'm the one
that decides when we're done here.

463
00:25:54.470 --> 00:25:56.840
Of course you are.cherie.
no offense intended.

464
00:25:56.860 --> 00:25:59.520
I'll be delivering the phone
records to Agent Perotta.

465
00:25:59.530 --> 00:26:01.200
I thought I'd do that in your office.

466
00:26:01.210 --> 00:26:03.350
Thanks.cherie.

467
00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:05.810
We're done.

468
00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:08.610
Well.we are done but that
was just a coincidence.

469
00:26:08.620 --> 00:26:10.950
Sweets.I've killed but
I've never murdered before.

470
00:26:10.960 --> 00:26:14.310
Look up the difference in your
little black book there.okay?

471
00:26:17.060 --> 00:26:18.520
This is legal.right?

472
00:26:18.530 --> 00:26:20.970
- Absolutely.
- Okay.

473
00:26:24.570 --> 00:26:26.490
None of them look nibbled on.

474
00:26:26.510 --> 00:26:30.840
Oh.man.they should've gone at each other like
a Peruvian soccer team stranded in the Andes.

475
00:26:31.670 --> 00:26:34.540
Then they all died at the same time.

476
00:26:37.520 --> 00:26:39.790
I don't see what this
is going to tell us.

477
00:26:39.800 --> 00:26:41.030
How they died.

478
00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:42.880
No.no.I mean about the case.

479
00:26:42.910 --> 00:26:47.230
Ooh.if Brennan were here.
she'd smack your face.

480
00:26:47.240 --> 00:26:52.060
Her philosophy is. we find out the facts about
everything. then see how it fits together.

481
00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:56.920
Photo opportunity.

482
00:26:59.320 --> 00:27:02.980
Pete made eight calls right
after the game to the same number.

483
00:27:03.520 --> 00:27:04.850
Lou Herrin. Who's that?

484
00:27:04.860 --> 00:27:06.340
A sergeant in the State Cops.

485
00:27:06.350 --> 00:27:08.830
He exchanged blows with the
victim the night that he died.

486
00:27:08.850 --> 00:27:11.210
Make it official. Question the cop.

487
00:27:11.220 --> 00:27:12.850
Let's get some leverage
on the guy first.

488
00:27:12.870 --> 00:27:15.640
Put him at the murder scene.
get a warrant to test his DNA.

489
00:27:15.650 --> 00:27:16.660
Here we go.

490
00:27:16.680 --> 00:27:20.030
Get a warrant for this.Ms.
Julian. get a warrant for that.

491
00:27:20.050 --> 00:27:22.330
You need grounds for a warrant.cherie.

492
00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:24.180
Don't they teach that
at Quantico anymore?

493
00:27:24.220 --> 00:27:27.290
What grounds have you got for
that warrant? None! Nothing!

494
00:27:27.300 --> 00:27:29.410
You're just wishing.

495
00:27:31.380 --> 00:27:33.380
I know how to get some
blood out of this Herrin.

496
00:27:33.390 --> 00:27:35.880
- Legally?
- Yeah.of course legally.

497
00:27:35.890 --> 00:27:36.860
How?

498
00:27:36.870 --> 00:27:39.470
Well.it's a big game tonight.right?

499
00:27:39.480 --> 00:27:42.740
And sometimes during
a game... people bleed.

500
00:27:45.020 --> 00:27:46.040
I don't like it.

501
00:27:46.050 --> 00:27:47.980
Then you don't have to show up.

502
00:28:02.060 --> 00:28:04.270
- What are you doing.man?
- What does it look like I'm doing?

503
00:28:04.670 --> 00:28:06.830
You think that's a good idea? You got
another couple of weeks on that cast.

504
00:28:06.840 --> 00:28:10.080
Well.considering I can't play with
a cast. then yeah.it's a great idea.

505
00:28:10.290 --> 00:28:11.920
You clear about the plan?

506
00:28:11.950 --> 00:28:15.600
Somebody bleeds. I collect a sample. put
it in a bag. pass it off to Dr. Brennan.

507
00:28:15.620 --> 00:28:18.050
Lou Herrin.number five.
he's our prime suspect.

508
00:28:18.060 --> 00:28:20.180
And I gotta make him bleed.

509
00:28:23.080 --> 00:28:25.900
You've worked with Booth
for a while now.right?

510
00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:30.690
Is he the kind of guy
that.uh. you know.I...

511
00:28:31.340 --> 00:28:34.300
Is he flirty?

512
00:28:34.720 --> 00:28:35.680
Flirty?

513
00:28:35.690 --> 00:28:39.340
Would you say he twinkles
his eyes at all women?

514
00:28:39.350 --> 00:28:43.620
Twinkly eyes actually result
when the pupils dilate very wide

515
00:28:43.650 --> 00:28:48.100
which is an unconscious result of
intense interest or sexual attraction.

516
00:28:48.110 --> 00:28:51.490
- So.no.he doesn't twinkle at everyone?
- No.

517
00:28:51.890 --> 00:28:53.680
All right.

518
00:28:57.530 --> 00:28:59.060
- Is that the guy?
- That's him.

519
00:28:59.070 --> 00:29:01.300
Lou Herrin. number five.

520
00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:03.400
You think he even knows how to bleed?

521
00:29:03.410 --> 00:29:05.600
Just keep your head up.all right?

522
00:29:11.320 --> 00:29:13.410
Come on. you should've called that.

523
00:29:13.950 --> 00:29:16.210
Pass it up!

524
00:29:30.180 --> 00:29:31.920
Keep your head up.Herrin.

525
00:29:50.800 --> 00:29:51.870
Man.what's your problem?

526
00:29:51.890 --> 00:29:53.910
I got a little chip.all right?
Just play your hockey.pal.

527
00:29:53.920 --> 00:29:55.120
This guy's hard to get mad.

528
00:29:55.150 --> 00:29:57.920
Man.he's maybe the only
one who hasn't shed a drop.

529
00:30:08.670 --> 00:30:11.300
Stay out of my face!
Keep your head up.huh!

530
00:30:17.010 --> 00:30:18.920
Take a warning.pal.

531
00:30:18.930 --> 00:30:21.340
I think I'm finally getting to this guy.

532
00:30:21.830 --> 00:30:24.140
Hope you survive it!

533
00:30:58.480 --> 00:31:00.940
Taking a little break?

534
00:31:03.740 --> 00:31:06.640
- Luc Robitaille?
- Seeley Booth.

535
00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:08.530
Right.

536
00:31:08.540 --> 00:31:10.640
Let's go.let's play.

537
00:31:11.080 --> 00:31:13.410
Right.

538
00:31:15.530 --> 00:31:17.350
You're the greatest
left-winger of all time.

539
00:31:17.360 --> 00:31:19.500
And you're the best player on your team.

540
00:31:19.510 --> 00:31:21.560
For what that's worth.

541
00:31:24.840 --> 00:31:27.780
All right.let's go. Come on.let's play.

542
00:31:31.370 --> 00:31:35.150
Here we go. Come on.show me something!

543
00:31:39.090 --> 00:31:42.040
Hey.come on.move.move!
Move.move.let's go!

544
00:31:45.440 --> 00:31:48.620
Whoa.wait a second. I can't play
hockey with you. I gotta solve a murder.

545
00:31:49.000 --> 00:31:51.020
You know.Booth...

546
00:31:52.390 --> 00:31:54.470
it's not about the blood.

547
00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:56.500
It's our best forensic clue.

548
00:31:56.800 --> 00:31:59.500
- Forget the blood.
- Then what?

549
00:31:59.510 --> 00:32:02.690
You know what makes a
team. Look at the team.

550
00:32:02.700 --> 00:32:04.760
It's about what brings a team together.

551
00:32:04.770 --> 00:32:07.970
The team. Look at the team.

552
00:32:07.980 --> 00:32:11.820
All right.let's go.one on one.
Let's see what you got. Come on.B.

553
00:32:18.010 --> 00:32:20.760
Geez.ugh. I thought I could
get by you there.you know?

554
00:32:20.770 --> 00:32:23.240
- You'll never get by me.
- Right.

555
00:32:23.250 --> 00:32:26.550
Now.listen.Booth. you're
not your father.okay?

556
00:32:26.560 --> 00:32:30.220
You protect the ones you care
about.on the ice and off the ice.

557
00:32:30.230 --> 00:32:32.350
That's who you are.

558
00:32:32.810 --> 00:32:36.110
You're not your father.
You're not your father.

559
00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:37.790
- Booth?
- You're not your father.

560
00:32:37.800 --> 00:32:39.230
Booth?

561
00:32:39.680 --> 00:32:41.660
Booth?

562
00:32:43.640 --> 00:32:45.310
Booth?

563
00:32:45.320 --> 00:32:47.330
Bones.what are you doing on the ice?

564
00:32:47.340 --> 00:32:50.400
I get nervous when you
fall down and don't get up.

565
00:32:50.870 --> 00:32:52.440
Come up here.

566
00:32:53.450 --> 00:32:55.820
- Up you go.buddy.
- Come on.

567
00:33:01.880 --> 00:33:03.950
Don't worry. I got the blood.

568
00:33:04.560 --> 00:33:07.290
- Good work.Bones.
- But I'm Bones.

569
00:33:15.670 --> 00:33:17.620
Smells like fish in here.

570
00:33:17.630 --> 00:33:20.510
Yep. It's the victim's goldfish.

571
00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:23.630
- They died of ammonia poisoning.
- How did that happen?

572
00:33:23.640 --> 00:33:28.310
I don't know. Maybe the victim washed his
aquarium with window cleaner? I don't know.

573
00:33:29.210 --> 00:33:31.490
How are things with you and Roxie?

574
00:33:31.840 --> 00:33:36.010
Uh.good... good.
Taking it slow.you know.

575
00:33:36.380 --> 00:33:38.800
Letting things unfold in a...

576
00:33:39.230 --> 00:33:40.370
Are you seeing anybody?

577
00:33:40.380 --> 00:33:44.930
I.um... actually went
out on a date last night.

578
00:33:45.720 --> 00:33:48.120
I'm glad to hear that.

579
00:33:48.140 --> 00:33:50.380
Any little twinge there?

580
00:33:51.020 --> 00:33:53.550
Definitely a little twinge. yeah.but...

581
00:33:53.560 --> 00:33:56.370
despite the twinge.I'm glad
you're back in the saddle.

582
00:33:56.390 --> 00:34:00.330
Oh.I'm not back in the saddle
exactly. It was just a first date.

583
00:34:00.340 --> 00:34:03.050
Barely got out of the barn.

584
00:34:04.300 --> 00:34:06.440
You saw the victim's apartment.right?

585
00:34:06.450 --> 00:34:08.940
Yes... yeah. Yeah.it was a pigsty.

586
00:34:08.950 --> 00:34:11.680
I don't think that guy cleaned anything.

587
00:34:11.690 --> 00:34:14.760
Not with ammonia. Not with anything.

588
00:34:17.290 --> 00:34:19.510
I came as soon as I heard
Booth had a brain injury.

589
00:34:19.520 --> 00:34:20.970
What part of your head hurts?

590
00:34:20.990 --> 00:34:22.250
The part above my shoulders.

591
00:34:22.270 --> 00:34:24.040
The doctor said he has a concussion.

592
00:34:24.070 --> 00:34:25.270
He shouldn't fall asleep.

593
00:34:25.290 --> 00:34:27.010
Otherwise. not serious.

594
00:34:27.020 --> 00:34:28.600
Tell him about the hallucination.

595
00:34:28.620 --> 00:34:29.650
You hallucinated?

596
00:34:29.660 --> 00:34:33.100
Luc Robitaille gave me advice.

597
00:34:34.100 --> 00:34:37.200
You got advice on a murder case from...

598
00:34:37.210 --> 00:34:38.270
What did he say?

599
00:34:38.300 --> 00:34:41.440
He said."Don't worry about
the... the player's blood."

600
00:34:42.950 --> 00:34:44.120
That's very interesting.

601
00:34:44.150 --> 00:34:46.060
Lucky Luc told me to look
in a different direction.

602
00:34:46.070 --> 00:34:46.930
That's interesting.

603
00:34:46.950 --> 00:34:48.370
Stop saying that... just stop.

604
00:34:48.380 --> 00:34:53.130
Preliminary DNA tests show that the blood mixed
in with the victim's did not belong to Lou Herrin.

605
00:34:53.150 --> 00:34:54.480
Lucky Luc was right.

606
00:34:54.490 --> 00:34:57.690
All that means is that you got
your brains scrambled for nothing.

607
00:34:57.700 --> 00:34:59.220
Lucky Luc is never wrong.

608
00:34:59.230 --> 00:35:03.730
This hallucination could be.uh. Booth's
subconscious speaking to him through the voice

609
00:35:03.770 --> 00:35:05.960
and image of someone that he idolizes.

610
00:35:05.990 --> 00:35:08.700
Like a modern version of a Vision Quest?

611
00:35:08.710 --> 00:35:11.860
You know what. hallucination or not...

612
00:35:12.770 --> 00:35:16.680
Lucky Luc.he told me
something about myself that...

613
00:35:20.740 --> 00:35:22.160
He told me something.

614
00:35:22.180 --> 00:35:24.700
I'd be very interested
in knowing what he said.

615
00:35:24.730 --> 00:35:30.360
Lucky for me.you're never gonna find out because
Bones is gonna drive me home and get me soup.

616
00:35:34.370 --> 00:35:37.990
There has got to be some reason
these fish died of ammonia poison.

617
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:41.450
Last time I did this. I ended up
in juvie hall over the weekend.

618
00:35:41.460 --> 00:35:43.450
- What?
- What?

619
00:35:43.460 --> 00:35:45.250
Uh.nothing.

620
00:35:52.850 --> 00:35:54.980
Buried treasure.

621
00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:57.850
What do we do now?

622
00:35:58.180 --> 00:36:01.980
Find out why the hell he was
hiding jewelry in a fish tank.

623
00:36:04.630 --> 00:36:07.630
Have any of you ever heard of
something called "chain of evidence"?

624
00:36:07.640 --> 00:36:08.680
Ms. Julian...

625
00:36:08.690 --> 00:36:11.300
Why didn't you go with these
two idiots to the victim's home?

626
00:36:11.320 --> 00:36:12.800
Please don't call my people idiots.

627
00:36:12.810 --> 00:36:14.060
We're not idiots.

628
00:36:14.080 --> 00:36:15.010
I feel like an idiot.

629
00:36:15.020 --> 00:36:18.070
You don't speak right
now-- neither of you.

630
00:36:18.380 --> 00:36:19.750
It's a crime scene.

631
00:36:19.780 --> 00:36:22.200
My people are very often at
crime scenes. It's what we do.

632
00:36:22.210 --> 00:36:23.420
No.it's not.

633
00:36:23.440 --> 00:36:27.180
You've got it in your heads
that you're crime scene types.

634
00:36:27.190 --> 00:36:29.620
This is Booth's fault for
indulging your fantasies.

635
00:36:29.640 --> 00:36:32.970
You are not crime scene
types. You are lab rats.

636
00:36:32.980 --> 00:36:34.520
No chain of evidence was broken.

637
00:36:34.560 --> 00:36:38.050
When Dr. Hodgins and Mr. Bray found
the items. they immediately called me.

638
00:36:38.080 --> 00:36:42.320
I called Booth. and when his head hurt too
much to talk to me. I called Agent Perotta.

639
00:36:42.340 --> 00:36:44.000
- Ms. Julian...
- What?

640
00:36:44.010 --> 00:36:46.090
A photograph of dead
fish led them to this.

641
00:36:46.110 --> 00:36:48.990
I think that kind of
brilliance is worth it.

642
00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:53.640
You've been taken hostage
by the squints.Agent Perotta.

643
00:36:55.340 --> 00:36:59.150
Turns out these items were
reported destroyed in a fire.

644
00:36:59.170 --> 00:37:01.230
The victim was a fireman.

645
00:37:01.250 --> 00:37:03.700
The FBI could check to see if
the Firedawgs put out that fire.

646
00:37:03.730 --> 00:37:06.780
Stole from the fire.
cleaned off with ammonia.

647
00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:08.790
Hidden in the aquarium. killed the fish.

648
00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:11.660
Okay. Now youarestraying
out of your territory.

649
00:37:11.670 --> 00:37:14.140
No.they got it right.

650
00:37:14.150 --> 00:37:18.650
The bracelet Agents Booth and Perotta
recovered from the victim's loan shark

651
00:37:18.660 --> 00:37:22.640
was reported destroyed
by that same fire.

652
00:37:23.160 --> 00:37:24.830
My people were right.

653
00:37:24.860 --> 00:37:25.930
Your people?

654
00:37:25.940 --> 00:37:28.150
We're Booth's people.

655
00:38:05.870 --> 00:38:10.830
They're on the Firedawgs. but they also
played on the same high school team.

656
00:38:10.840 --> 00:38:14.040
What brings them together.eh?

657
00:38:15.070 --> 00:38:16.830
I'm back.

658
00:38:16.840 --> 00:38:19.000
Hey.what brings them together?

659
00:38:19.010 --> 00:38:21.110
What brings the team together?

660
00:38:21.120 --> 00:38:22.730
So.I got the soup from the place.

661
00:38:22.740 --> 00:38:27.060
And.yes.I told Mama that
it was for you especially.

662
00:38:28.520 --> 00:38:31.430
It's all about the
team there. It's all...

663
00:38:33.510 --> 00:38:35.460
- What are you doing?
- It's all about the team there.

664
00:38:35.470 --> 00:38:37.770
Bones.it's all about
the team there. They...

665
00:38:38.480 --> 00:38:41.580
these four guys...they all played
hockey together in high school.

666
00:38:41.590 --> 00:38:45.890
and now they all play
together as a team.

667
00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:49.650
- They're all firemen?
- Yeah. They all worked the jewelry store fire.

668
00:38:50.070 --> 00:38:52.620
One of these three guys is the murderer.

669
00:38:52.630 --> 00:38:54.770
According to Mr. Lucky?

670
00:38:55.960 --> 00:39:01.040
It's Luc.okay? It is... it... it's
not Mr. Lucky. It is Luc Robitaille.

671
00:39:01.050 --> 00:39:03.710
Left wing. Great shot.

672
00:39:03.720 --> 00:39:06.040
Luc Robitaille-- he's one of
the best left wings of all time.

673
00:39:06.050 --> 00:39:08.270
What is this?

674
00:39:08.280 --> 00:39:09.850
It's a lace puller. Why?

675
00:39:09.860 --> 00:39:12.860
I think it might be the murder weapon.

676
00:39:14.500 --> 00:39:16.720
We want to discuss
the jewelry store fire.

677
00:39:16.730 --> 00:39:18.440
- I want a lawyer.
- What for.Alex?

678
00:39:18.450 --> 00:39:20.310
We didn't do anything
wrong. None of us did.

679
00:39:20.320 --> 00:39:21.290
What about Pete?

680
00:39:21.320 --> 00:39:24.120
He break some kind of fireman
code.something like that?

681
00:39:24.130 --> 00:39:25.160
Yeah.something like that.

682
00:39:25.180 --> 00:39:27.890
I've got nothing to say about
any of this. I want a lawyer.

683
00:39:27.900 --> 00:39:30.410
We know Carlson was
beaten with a hockey stick.

684
00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:34.900
after which a lace puller entered his
brain through his eye and killed him.

685
00:39:34.940 --> 00:39:37.230
What about your dream.Ed?

686
00:39:37.240 --> 00:39:39.910
You were gonna play for the NHL.right?

687
00:39:39.920 --> 00:39:44.190
"Local player scouted by
the NHL." Look at that one.

688
00:39:44.200 --> 00:39:45.880
Oh.this one's good.too.

689
00:39:45.890 --> 00:39:48.640
"Fralic's hat trick wins game."

690
00:39:50.100 --> 00:39:51.120
I got injured.

691
00:39:51.130 --> 00:39:55.640
This injury would end any chance
of a career in professional hockey.

692
00:39:55.650 --> 00:39:57.060
What does that have to do with anything?

693
00:39:57.090 --> 00:40:00.210
Look.I got hurt. now I sell siding.
and I play hockey on the weekends.

694
00:40:00.240 --> 00:40:02.310
Why you got to rub his face in the past?

695
00:40:02.330 --> 00:40:04.410
Who ruined you?

696
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:08.350
Pete Carlson.

697
00:40:09.960 --> 00:40:12.000
It was Pete.

698
00:40:12.010 --> 00:40:13.650
You all knew about the stolen jewelry.

699
00:40:13.660 --> 00:40:15.930
The question is.how many of you
were there the night he was killed?

700
00:40:15.940 --> 00:40:19.310
None of us. Nobody here had
anything to do with that.

701
00:40:19.320 --> 00:40:24.040
We have the hockey stick.
the murder weapon and DNA.

702
00:40:24.060 --> 00:40:25.830
It's only a matter of time.

703
00:40:34.940 --> 00:40:37.740
- Yeah.
- What?

704
00:40:37.750 --> 00:40:39.650
It was me.

705
00:40:39.660 --> 00:40:42.820
I asked to meet Pete on the
ice after everybody left.

706
00:40:42.830 --> 00:40:46.970
I told him to give back the stolen
jewelry. and he said to me...

707
00:40:49.260 --> 00:40:53.370
He said to me that I was a... a coward.

708
00:40:54.960 --> 00:40:59.330
That I didn't do anything to him back
in the day when he wrecked my life

709
00:40:59.720 --> 00:41:02.580
and I wouldn't do anything to him now.

710
00:41:05.610 --> 00:41:08.400
Well.he was wrong.

711
00:41:29.620 --> 00:41:32.600
I'm not positive this is a good idea.

712
00:41:32.610 --> 00:41:37.080
Oh.I got you! I got you. Stay up here.
Okay.it's all right. Here we go. one more.

713
00:41:37.090 --> 00:41:39.110
Well.you know what.I
got to stay up all night.

714
00:41:39.130 --> 00:41:42.070
so who better to keep
me company than you?

715
00:41:42.100 --> 00:41:46.010
You and me skating is saving
you from slipping into a coma?

716
00:41:46.760 --> 00:41:49.430
Oh.easy.Bones. NowI'mgonna go down.

717
00:41:49.440 --> 00:41:51.610
I have a lot of natural
athletic ability.

718
00:41:51.640 --> 00:41:54.360
Oh.yeah.natural. I
can... I can see that.

719
00:41:54.370 --> 00:41:58.050
Real smooth and natural.
That's it. Well done.

720
00:42:01.200 --> 00:42:05.710
That Agent Perotta. she
really enjoyed working with us.

721
00:42:06.050 --> 00:42:07.720
Yeah.

722
00:42:07.730 --> 00:42:09.560
But.um...

723
00:42:10.580 --> 00:42:13.430
you're the only FBI
